  "mathematical_scope_statement": {
    "formally_proved_in_lean": [
      "Finite graded conflict-clause poset L_3 (27 clauses across Layers 0, 1, 2, 3; 54 covering edges; reflexivity, transitivity, antisymmetry of implication order; bounded meet-semilattice laws in ConflictClauseLattice/PosetLattice.lean, 25 theorems).",
      "Cellular chain complex over Z (boundary_1 o boundary_2 = 0, boundary_2 o boundary_3 = 0, Euler-Poincare identity 1 - 6 + 12 - 8 = -1, and exact #3-SAT unobstructed dual-atom bijection in ConflictClauseLattice/HomologicalCertificate.lean, 18 theorems).",
      "Pure functional step-counting monad (CountM := StateM CountingState) with tick transitions, Monad Reduction (simp [Bind.bind, StateT.bind]), State Injection (injection), discrete Presburger arithmetic step bounds (omega) for simulateLatticeTraversal (<= n^2 + 2^n) and simulateBlockHomologicalTraversal (<= (n+m)^2 + 2^(n/max(k,1))), and real-valued sub-exponential bounds over Real using Mathlib's Real.log and Real.rpow (block_homological_traversal_real_log_bound, simulateBlockHomologicalTraversal_at_logBlockSize_bound, subExponential_rpow_lt_two_pow, and simulateLatticeTraversal_exceeds_subExponential_bound in ConflictClauseLattice/StepCountingMonad.lean, 24 theorems).",
      "Master 5-pillar conjunction theorem (eth_conflict_clause_lattice_master_product_theorem in ConflictClauseLattice/FinalProductTheorem.lean, 1 theorem)."
    ],
    "model_assumptions_and_boundaries": [
      "The CountM step-counting monad tracks exact tick counts of pure functional Lean cost models (simulateLatticeTraversal and simulateBlockHomologicalTraversal parameterized by (n, m, blockK)); it does not measure physical wall-clock runtime or compiler-emitted machine instructions, and does not prove an unconditional block-rank decomposition for arbitrary coupled n-variable 3-CNF boundary matrices."
    ]
  }
